## Third-party content

The files under `skills/` are redistributed verbatim and are not covered by the
copyright above.

### `skills/ponytail*/SKILL.md`

Verbatim from [DietrichGebert/ponytail](https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail)
at tag `v4.10.0`, verified byte-identical. MIT, © Dietrich Gebert.

### `skills/grill-me/SKILL.md`

This one file has a chain of ancestry; no single upstream is its author.

1. **Verbatim source.** Byte-identical to npm
   [`dsh-grill-me@0.1.0`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-grill-me), which is
   MIT-licensed and © chensatan13. That package declares a GitHub repository
   (`satan9394/dsh-grill-me`) that is not publicly reachable, so npm is cited as
   the source of record.
2. **That package's stated inspiration.** Its README credits
   [RobMitt/grill-me-skill](https://github.com/robmitt/grill-me-skill). Seven
   substantive sentences in the body are verbatim from that repo's `SKILL.md`
   (the `AskUserQuestion` instructions, the "one question at a time" rule, the
   "Other field" note, the codebase-lookup rule, and the closing summary rule).
   **That repository carries no LICENSE file**, so it is "all rights reserved"
   by default — see the note below.
3. **Where the description text comes from.** RobMitt's frontmatter
   `description` line (244 bytes) is byte-identical to the same line in
   [mattpocock/skills](https://github.com/mattpocock/skills) at commit
   `62f43a18`, added there on 2026-03-13 in `d1beb4fe`. Matt Pocock's repo is
   MIT, © 2026 Matt Pocock. The design-tree framing originates there too
   (RobMitt's repo was created 2026-04-11, after that text already existed).

So the honest position is: the **DSH-specific mechanics** (one question at a
time, driving `ask_user_question`, the "what to grill about" checklist) are what
this port actually contributes, and the **prose underneath descends from Matt
Pocock's MIT-licensed original via an unlicensed intermediate**.

### Licensing caveat

Because step 2 above is a repository with no license, the provenance of some
sentences in `skills/grill-me/SKILL.md` is not clean. This file is included
here for transparency and local use; if you intend to redistribute this bundle
commercially, replace `skills/grill-me/SKILL.md` with your own text first. The
mechanism it drives (see `README.md`) is independent of the wording.

### Original work

Only the DSH integration — `index.js`, `lib/`, `cordis.patch.yml`, `test/` — is
original work.
